### Week 4 REST Client tests
### Run database.sql first so the table starts as rows 1-3.
### Then run these requests from top to bottom (click "Send Request" above each one).

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3001

### 1. Database health -> 200, databaseTime returned
GET {{baseUrl}}/health/database

### 2. GET all -> 200, JSON array
GET {{baseUrl}}/movies

### 3. GET existing -> 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/movies/1

### 4. GET missing -> 404
GET {{baseUrl}}/movies/9999

### 5. GET invalid id -> 400
GET {{baseUrl}}/movies/abc

### 6. POST valid -> 201, id generated by PostgreSQL (4 after a fresh database.sql)
POST {{baseUrl}}/movies
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "title": "Arrival",
    "director": "Denis Villeneuve",
    "year": 2016
}

### 7. POST invalid (missing director, year is a string) -> 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/movies
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "title": "No Director",
    "year": "2020"
}

### 8. PUT complete -> 200, every field replaced
PUT {{baseUrl}}/movies/4
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "title": "Dune",
    "director": "Denis Villeneuve",
    "year": 2021
}

### 9. PUT incomplete (no year) -> 400
PUT {{baseUrl}}/movies/4
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "title": "Dune",
    "director": "Denis Villeneuve"
}

### 10. PUT missing movie -> 404
PUT {{baseUrl}}/movies/9999
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "title": "Ghost",
    "director": "Nobody",
    "year": 2000
}

### 11. PATCH one field -> 200, only title changes
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/movies/4
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "title": "Dune: Part One"
}

### 12. PATCH empty body -> 400
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/movies/4
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### 13. PATCH unknown field (not in allow-list) -> 400
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/movies/4
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "id": 100
}

### 14. DELETE existing -> 204, no body
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/movies/4

### 15. DELETE same movie again -> 404
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/movies/4

### 16. GET deleted movie -> 404
GET {{baseUrl}}/movies/4

### 17. Filter by director (case-insensitive) -> 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/movies?director=christopher nolan

### 18. Filter by year -> 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/movies?year=1999

### 19. Sort by year (oldest first) -> 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/movies?sortBy=year

### 20. Sort by title descending -> 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/movies?sortBy=title&order=desc

### 21. Sort by a column not in the allow-list -> 400
GET {{baseUrl}}/movies?sortBy=release_year;DROP TABLE movies

### 22. SQL injection attempt as a filter value -> 200, empty array (treated as plain text)
GET {{baseUrl}}/movies?director=' OR '1'='1

### ---- Persistence test (Task 6.2) ----
### a) Send this POST, b) check it in pgAdmin, c) stop Express with Ctrl+C,
### d) start it again with npm start, e) send the GET below. The movie is still there.

### 23. POST persistence movie -> 201
POST {{baseUrl}}/movies
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "title": "Persistence Test Movie",
    "director": "Your Name",
    "year": 2026
}

### 24. After restarting Express: GET all -> the movie from step 23 is still listed
GET {{baseUrl}}/movies
